  "summary": "At a town hall hosted by Toledo Councilman Erin Kramer, residents raised privacy and transparency concerns about the city's Flock Safety cameras. Council leaders have introduced legislation for an independent audit of the system, with a possible vote as early as Sept. 22, following a June 8-4 vote to extend the Flock contract for one year.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "Ms. Kramer then said the council is aware of residential concerns about the city's Flock cameras and is requesting an independent audit of them to ensure the technology is being used appropriately.",
      "paragraph_idx": 8
    },
    {
      "quote": "The audit legislation she referenced Wednesday was formally introduced Tuesday by Council President Vanice Williams and Councilman John Hobbs III, following an 8-4 vote in June to extend the Flock contract for one year.",
      "paragraph_idx": 10
    }
  ],
